<fieldset><legend>Performance Dashboard</legend>
  <p><label for="settings_performance_delivery_target">Delivery Target (%)</label><%= number_field_tag 'settings[performance_delivery_target]', TicketJourney::PerformanceSettings.delivery_target(settings), id: 'settings_performance_delivery_target', min: 0, max: 100, step: 'any', required: true %> Default: 90%. Shared by Done Tickets / Due Tickets and Done Weight / Due Weight for all employees and projects. Changes also apply to past report dates; actual delivery percentages are unchanged.</p>
  <p>Configure existing numeric User custom fields. Create each field only if it does not already exist. No fields are created automatically.</p>
  <p>Both monthly metrics use the last three completed calendar months before the selected report date's month. Ticket totals and usable complexity weights are divided by 3, including months with no deliveries. No Day 0 configuration is required; account creation, ticket Start dates, and the former manual setting do not change this window.</p>
  <% [['count', 'Expected Monthly Ticket Count'], ['weight', 'Expected Monthly Complexity Weight']].each do |key, label| %>
    <p><label for="settings_performance_<%= key %>_field_id"><%= label %></label><%= select_tag "settings[performance_#{key}_field_id]", options_for_select(UserCustomField.where(field_format: %w[int float]).order(:name).map { |f| ["#{f.name} (##{f.id})", f.id] }, settings["performance_#{key}_field_id"]), include_blank: 'Not configured', id: "settings_performance_#{key}_field_id" %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p>Only public monthly target fields are shown to non-administrators. Monthly employee targets are separate from the shared delivery percentage. No Extra Tasks adjustment applies.</p>
</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Periodic Time — Targets</legend>
  <p>Initial targets: normal DTC 7 calendar days, priority DTC 3 calendar days, Development to Total Ticket Time Estimation Ratio 90%. Blank or unset values use these defaults; explicit configured values are preserved. Current settings also apply to past reports. Activity observations do not overwrite targets automatically.</p>
  <% [['performance_periodic_dtc_target', 'Normal Tickets DTC target (calendar days)'], ['performance_periodic_priority_dtc_target', 'Priority Tickets DTC target (calendar days)'], ['performance_periodic_owner_share', 'Development to Total Ticket Time Estimation Ratio (%)']].each do |key, label| %>
    <p><%= label_tag "settings_#{key}", label %><%= number_field_tag "settings[#{key}]", TicketJourney::PerformanceSettings.periodic_target(settings, key), id: "settings_#{key}", min: 0, max: (100 if key.end_with?('owner_share')), step: 'any' %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p><strong>Development activity classification:</strong> only activities named Development qualify, including project-specific versions. QA, Review, Deployment and other activities remain separate. Existing matching records: <%= TicketJourney::PerformanceSettings.development_activities.order(:id).map { |activity| "#{activity.name} (##{activity.id})" }.join(', ').presence || 'None — development ratios unavailable' %>. New project-specific Development records are included automatically.</p>
</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Performance Time — Working Calendar and Thresholds</legend>
  <% calendar = TicketJourney::WorkingCalendar.new(settings) %>
  <p><label>Working weekdays</label><%= hidden_field_tag 'settings[performance_working_weekdays][]', '', id: nil %>
    <% [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 0].each do |day| %>
      <label class="inline"><%= check_box_tag 'settings[performance_working_weekdays][]', day, calendar.weekdays.include?(day), id: "performance_workday_#{day}" %> <%= Date::DAYNAMES[day] %></label>
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <p><label for="settings_performance_hours_per_day">Default working hours per day</label><%= number_field_tag 'settings[performance_hours_per_day]', calendar.hours_per_day, id: 'settings_performance_hours_per_day', min: 0.01, max: 24, step: 'any', required: true %> Default: 8.</p>
  <p><label for="settings_performance_holidays">Organization holidays</label><%= text_area_tag 'settings[performance_holidays]', settings['performance_holidays'], id: 'settings_performance_holidays', rows: 6, cols: 48 %><br>One date per line: YYYY-MM-DD followed by an optional description. These dates are excluded from working time and age.</p>
  <p><label for="settings_performance_weekly_hours_field_id">Owner weekly-hours field</label><%= select_tag 'settings[performance_weekly_hours_field_id]', options_for_select(UserCustomField.where(field_format: %w[int float]).order(:name).map { |field| ["#{field.name} (##{field.id})", field.id] }, settings['performance_weekly_hours_field_id']), include_blank: 'Use default daily hours', id: 'settings_performance_weekly_hours_field_id' %><br>Optional existing numeric User field; no field is created. Weekly hours divide by configured working weekdays. Missing, hidden or invalid values fall back to default daily hours and are disclosed in the report. Private values are never exposed to non-administrators.</p>
  <% [['performance_estimate_allowance', 'Estimate overrun allowance (%)'], ['performance_sv_warning', 'SV warning threshold (%)']].each do |key, label| %>
    <p><label for="settings_<%= key %>"><%= label %></label><%= number_field_tag "settings[#{key}]", TicketJourney::PerformanceSettings.time_threshold(settings, key), id: "settings_#{key}", min: 0, max: 100, step: 'any', required: true %> Default: 10%.</p>
  <% end %>
  <p>Age is zero on the Start Date and counts working days after it. SV includes the report day's full scheduled working hours. Pauses are included. Current settings also apply to past report dates; calendar edits can change historical results. Owner-specific daily hours cancel out of the elapsed/window fraction when constant across the schedule; they do not change the ticket's PM Estimate.</p>
</fieldset>
